## Generic declarations and ordered match plans

Extend the first fragment with `TypeDecl`, representation-specific `CtorLayout`, and `MatchPlan` rather than adding another dedicated built-in data structure for each example. Begin with closed monomorphic nominal recursive groups, including mutual references. Resolve declaration/constructor/field/binder identities, construct a plain tagged layout and compile ordered pattern matrices using first-column specialization/default decomposition. Generic parameters need a separately bounded instantiation policy; finite declarations alone do not bound specialization or recursive value sizes.

The scrutinee evaluates once; constructor fields evaluate once in source order. Match selection returns the earliest matching source arm, binds fields in its arm environment, executes only that body and restores the saved outer environment. Occurrence paths are semantic field paths, not arena addresses. `NoMatch` is a plan/helper result mapping to `Rejected(error9)`, not a new application outcome, under the Opus-owned reconciliation. `MatchPlan.workMap` retains reference events/stop positions even when physical tests or suffixes share work. Heuristic columns, unboxing and layout packing follow comparison against direct ordered matching and the plain plan.

A specified normal discriminator is `Schedule = Done | Pay(UInt128,Schedule) | Both(Schedule,Schedule)`. Ordered arms `Both(Pay(x,_),_) -> x; Both(_,r) -> sum(r); Pay(x,t) -> x+sum(t); Done -> 0` give 4 on `Both(Pay(4,Done),Pay(5,Done))`; a structural sum gives 9. Shared/unshared `Both(Pay(4,Done),Pay(4,Done))` both sum to 8 with two occurrences. These are new unexecuted extension cases. Higher-order closures, arbitrary letrec values, GADTs, mutable/cyclic data, or-patterns, indirect bytecode and foreign VMs remain explicit further extensions, not implied support.

## Financial suspension and existing Core/2

EXACT REGION openspec/changes/sherlock-universal-interpreter-design/interfaces.md L293-L307; sourceSHA256=bee739da090c41230adc6ebd711075d842ef127d7fed8d54276e9fb484d19536

```text
TypeDecl = {nominalId:TypeId,parameters,recursiveGroup,constructors:[CtorDecl]}
CtorDecl = {ctorId:CtorId,sourceOrder,fields:[{fieldId,type}]}
CtorLayout = {nominalId:TypeId,ctorId:CtorId,tag,fields:[{fieldId,type,slotKind}],width}
MatchPlan = {sourceMatchId:SourceOccurrenceId,scrutineeType:TypeId,
             nodes:[PlanNode],entry,armTable,workMap}
PlanNode = Switch(occurrencePath,cases,default) | Bind(binderId,occurrencePath,next)
         | Select(sourceArmId,bodyExprId) | NoMatch
```

`NoMatch` is a match-plan/helper result that maps to application `Rejected(error9)`, following the Opus-owned reconciliation; it adds no `Outcome` variant. The exact transition and full error-code table remain Phase 0 work.

First extend to closed monomorphic nominal recursive groups, including mutual references. Assign stable type/constructor/field/binder/occurrence IDs; derive a plain tagged-node layout; compile source-ordered pattern matrices using first-column specialization/default decomposition. Field slot `i` always means source field `i`. Evaluate constructor fields strictly left-to-right before allocation and the scrutinee once before matching. Select the minimum matching source arm index, bind in its fresh arm scope and execute only its body. Pattern occurrences use `(sourceMatchId,sourceArmId,fieldPath)`, never arena addresses. `workMap` carries an ordered reference-event cursor; shared tests/suffixes cannot erase charges or stop positions. Heuristic columns, packing and test sharing are later comparisons. Parameterized types need separately bounded instantiation; closures, GADTs, mutation/cycles and or-patterns remain additional extensions. Existing dedicated K list/tree sorts do not discharge this work.


